% Refractive Lenses: LCD L33793 and its Policy Article A52499 (DME MACs). A
% policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le (orders,
% delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills) and states when a
% claim for an eyeglass lens (the V2100–V2499, V2700 and V2770 lens codes
% the Article lists), a contact lens (V2520–V2524, V2531), standard frames
% (V2020) or a lens add-on (the V2115–V2797 add-on codes the Article lists)
% is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY. The benefit is not durable medical
% equipment: the Policy Article places refractive lenses under the
% Prosthetic Devices benefit of Social Security Act §1861(s)(8), so no
% condition on the place of use applies. The items the Article denies as
% noncovered — deluxe frames (V2025), deluxe lens features (V2702),
% scratch resistant, mirror and polarized coatings (V2760, V2761, V2762),
% progressive lenses (V2781), high index lenses (V2782, V2783), specialty
% occupational lenses (V2786), eyeglass cases (V2756), low vision aids
% (V2600, V2610, V2615) and the components of another code (V2797) — are
% in scope but in no benefit.
%
% The coverage criteria:
%   1. a covered diagnosis — the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is in
%      the Article's ICD-10 table (sources/icd10/A52499_icd10_covered.csv,
%      6 rows, loaded as the table refractive_lenses_icd10; its one group,
%      group 1, serves every code of the policy): pseudophakia (Z96.1,
%      "Presence of intraocular lens"), aphakia and congenital aphakia
%      (the other five rows);
%   2. for a pseudophakic beneficiary, one pair of eyeglasses or contact
%      lenses after each cataract surgery with insertion of an intraocular
%      lens: the surgeries and the pairs furnished are dated facts of the
%      record, and a pair is covered when some surgery has had no pair
%      furnished after it (so two surgeries with no pair between them yield
%      one pair, after the second, and replacements are not covered);
%   3. for an aphakic beneficiary, the lenses or combinations of lenses the
%      LCD lists are covered when determined to be medically necessary, and
%      so are replacements: a judgment, the finding "lenses medically
%      necessary" (which of the combinations is worn is not modelled);
%   4. frames and add-ons only with a covered lens — the frame or add-on is
%      an accessory of the lens (the shared template);
%   5. anti-reflective coating (V2750), tints (V2744, V2745) and oversize
%      lenses (V2780) only when the treating practitioner documents their
%      medical necessity (a fact of the record), and tints not as
%      sunglasses in addition to regular prosthetic lenses; UV coating
%      (V2755) is reasonable and necessary after cataract extraction but not
%      on a polycarbonate lens (V2784, another add-on of the same lens);
%      polycarbonate (V2784) only for a beneficiary with functional vision
%      in only one eye.
%
% The payment condition the Policy Article adds ("Policy specific
% documentation requirements"), in section remedy: the diagnosis code that
% justifies the need for the item is on the claim (the template of
% afo_kafo.le, a candidate for dmepos.le).
%
% Not modelled: the KX, GA, GY, GZ, RT and LT modifiers and the billing of
% deluxe frames and progressive lenses on two lines (billing rules); the
% coding of the PROSE device (V2627 or V2531 by the condition treated);
% contact lenses used as a corneal dressing (V2520–V2523 are then
% noncovered — no record fact distinguishes the use); that the lenses of a
% pair are two claim lines (each lens is a claim of its own, and a pair
% previously furnished is one dated fact).

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    *a beneficiary* had a cataract extraction with insertion of an intraocular lens on *a date*; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* was furnished a pair of eyeglasses or contact lenses on *a date*; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* has functional vision in only one eye; undefined.
    the treating practitioner documented the medical necessity of *an item* for *a beneficiary*; undefined.
    *an item* is used as sunglasses in addition to regular prosthetic lenses; undefined.
    % candidate for dmepos.le (also a template of afo_kafo.le and knee_orthoses.le)
    *a claim* states the diagnosis code of the beneficiary; undefined.
    % the codes and the table
    ICD10 code *a code* is in group *a group* of article *an article* as *a description* under table refractive_lenses_icd10.
    code *a code* is excluded from the refractive lenses benefit.
    % derived
    *an item* is an eyeglass lens.
    *an item* is a contact lens.
    *an item* is a refractive lens.
    *an item* is a lens add-on.
    *a beneficiary* has a covered diagnosis for refractive lenses.
    *a beneficiary* is pseudophakic.
    *a beneficiary* is aphakic.
    *a beneficiary* is entitled to a pair of lenses after cataract surgery on *a date*.
    *a beneficiary* was furnished a pair of lenses after *a date*.
    *an item* is a covered refractive lens for *a beneficiary*.
    *an item* is an add-on of a covered lens for *a beneficiary*.
    *a device* carries an impact resistant add-on.

% The Article's ICD-10 table: the covered diagnoses (group 1, the only
% group; the CSV columns bind to the template's arguments in order: code,
% group, article, description).
the table refractive_lenses_icd10 is loaded from sources/icd10/A52499_icd10_covered.csv, with all matches:
    code | group | article | description

the knowledge base refractive_lenses includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base refractive_lenses includes:

LCD L33793 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33793".
the text of LCD L33793 is at "sources/lcd/L33793.txt".
Policy Article A52499 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52499".
the text of Policy Article A52499 is at "sources/article/A52499.txt".

% What the items are, by code (Policy Article A52499, coding guidelines).
rule lenses_eyeglass with provenance Policy Article A52499,
        confer "describe specific eyeglass lenses. Only one of these codes may be billed for each lens provided":
an item is an eyeglass lens
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["V2100", "V2101", "V2102", "V2103", "V2104", "V2105", "V2106", "V2107", "V2108", "V2109", "V2110", "V2111", "V2112", "V2113", "V2114", "V2199", "V2200", "V2201", "V2202", "V2203", "V2204", "V2205", "V2206", "V2207", "V2208", "V2209", "V2210", "V2211", "V2212", "V2213", "V2214", "V2299", "V2300", "V2301", "V2302", "V2303", "V2304", "V2305", "V2306", "V2307", "V2308", "V2309", "V2310", "V2311", "V2312", "V2313", "V2314", "V2399", "V2410", "V2430", "V2499", "V2700", "V2770"].

rule lenses_contact with provenance Policy Article A52499,
        confer "Code V2524 is used for any type of photochromatic contact lens":
an item is a contact lens
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["V2520", "V2521", "V2522", "V2523", "V2524", "V2531"].

% a refractive lens is an eyeglass lens or a contact lens: a device of this model
rule lenses_eyeglass_is_lens:
an item is a refractive lens
    if the item is an eyeglass lens.

rule lenses_contact_is_lens:
an item is a refractive lens
    if the item is a contact lens.

rule lenses_addon with provenance Policy Article A52499,
        confer "describe add-on features of lenses. They are billed in addition to codes for the basic lens":
an item is a lens add-on
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["V2115", "V2118", "V2121", "V2215", "V2218", "V2219", "V2220", "V2221", "V2315", "V2318", "V2319", "V2320", "V2321", "V2710", "V2715", "V2718", "V2730", "V2744", "V2745", "V2750", "V2755", "V2756", "V2760", "V2780", "V2781", "V2782", "V2783", "V2784", "V2786", "V2797"].

% A lens that is itself covered for its beneficiary, and an add-on of one.
% Devices of this model.
rule lenses_covered_lens:
an item is a covered refractive lens for a beneficiary
    if the item is a refractive lens
    and the item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and a claim is for the item
    and the claim is reasonable and necessary.

rule lenses_addon_of_covered:
an item is an add-on of a covered lens for a beneficiary
    if the item is a lens add-on
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the device is a covered refractive lens for the beneficiary.

rule lenses_impact_resistant_addon:
a device carries an impact resistant add-on
    if an item is an accessory of the device
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "V2784".

% A pair furnished after a surgery: a device of this model.
rule lenses_pair_after:
a beneficiary was furnished a pair of lenses after a date
    if the beneficiary was furnished a pair of eyeglasses or contact lenses on an other date
    and the other date is after the date.

section applicability is:

% The codes this policy decides: the lenses, the frames and the add-ons,
% including those the Article denies as noncovered.
rule lenses_codes with provenance Policy Article A52499,
        confer "The RT and/or LT modifiers must be used with all HCPCS codes in this policy except codes V2020, V2025 and V2600":
the policy for code a code is refractive_lenses
    if the code is in ["V2020", "V2025", "V2100", "V2101", "V2102", "V2103", "V2104", "V2105", "V2106", "V2107", "V2108", "V2109", "V2110", "V2111", "V2112", "V2113", "V2114", "V2115", "V2118", "V2121", "V2199", "V2200", "V2201", "V2202", "V2203", "V2204", "V2205", "V2206", "V2207", "V2208", "V2209", "V2210", "V2211", "V2212", "V2213", "V2214", "V2215", "V2218", "V2219", "V2220", "V2221", "V2299", "V2300", "V2301", "V2302", "V2303", "V2304", "V2305", "V2306", "V2307", "V2308", "V2309", "V2310", "V2311", "V2312", "V2313", "V2314", "V2315", "V2318", "V2319", "V2320", "V2321", "V2399", "V2410", "V2430", "V2499", "V2520", "V2521", "V2522", "V2523", "V2524", "V2531", "V2600", "V2610", "V2615", "V2700", "V2702", "V2710", "V2715", "V2718", "V2730", "V2744", "V2745", "V2750", "V2755", "V2756", "V2760", "V2761", "V2762", "V2770", "V2780", "V2781", "V2782", "V2783", "V2784", "V2786", "V2797"].

% The benefit: not durable medical equipment but the Prosthetic Devices
% benefit of Social Security Act §1861(s)(8) — for every code of the policy
% but those the Article puts outside it.
rule lenses_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52499,
        confer "Refractive lenses are covered under the prosthetic devices benefit category (Social Security Act §1861(s)(8))":
the benefit category of code a code is prosthetic devices
    if the policy for code the code is refractive_lenses
    and it is not the case that
        code the code is excluded from the refractive lenses benefit.

code "V2025" is excluded from the refractive lenses benefit,
    as stated in Policy Article A52499, confer "Additional charges for deluxe frames (V2025) will be denied as noncovered".
code "V2760" is excluded from the refractive lenses benefit,
    as stated in Policy Article A52499, confer "Scratch resistant coating (V2760), mirror coating (V2761), polarization (V2762), deluxe lens feature (V2702) and progressive lenses (V2781) will be denied as noncovered".
code "V2761" is excluded from the refractive lenses benefit,
    as stated in Policy Article A52499, confer "Scratch resistant coating (V2760), mirror coating (V2761), polarization (V2762), deluxe lens feature (V2702) and progressive lenses (V2781) will be denied as noncovered".
code "V2762" is excluded from the refractive lenses benefit,
    as stated in Policy Article A52499, confer "Scratch resistant coating (V2760), mirror coating (V2761), polarization (V2762), deluxe lens feature (V2702) and progressive lenses (V2781) will be denied as noncovered".
code "V2702" is excluded from the refractive lenses benefit,
    as stated in Policy Article A52499, confer "Scratch resistant coating (V2760), mirror coating (V2761), polarization (V2762), deluxe lens feature (V2702) and progressive lenses (V2781) will be denied as noncovered".
code "V2781" is excluded from the refractive lenses benefit,
    as stated in Policy Article A52499, confer "Scratch resistant coating (V2760), mirror coating (V2761), polarization (V2762), deluxe lens feature (V2702) and progressive lenses (V2781) will be denied as noncovered".
code "V2782" is excluded from the refractive lenses benefit,
    as stated in Policy Article A52499, confer "high index glass or plastic (V2782, V2783) for indications such as light weight or thinness will be denied as a noncovered deluxe feature".
code "V2783" is excluded from the refractive lenses benefit,
    as stated in Policy Article A52499, confer "high index glass or plastic (V2782, V2783) for indications such as light weight or thinness will be denied as a noncovered deluxe feature".
code "V2786" is excluded from the refractive lenses benefit,
    as stated in Policy Article A52499, confer "Specialty occupational multifocal lenses (V2786) will be denied as noncovered".
code "V2756" is excluded from the refractive lenses benefit,
    as stated in Policy Article A52499, confer "Eyeglass cases (V2756) will be denied as noncovered".
code "V2600" is excluded from the refractive lenses benefit,
    as stated in Policy Article A52499, confer "Low vision aids (V2600, V2610, V2615) will be denied as noncovered".
code "V2610" is excluded from the refractive lenses benefit,
    as stated in Policy Article A52499, confer "Low vision aids (V2600, V2610, V2615) will be denied as noncovered".
code "V2615" is excluded from the refractive lenses benefit,
    as stated in Policy Article A52499, confer "Low vision aids (V2600, V2610, V2615) will be denied as noncovered".
code "V2797" is excluded from the refractive lenses benefit,
    as stated in Policy Article A52499, confer "Vision supplies, accessories, and/or service components of another HCPCS vision code (V2797) will be denied as not separately payable".

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The claims: a lens for a pseudophakic or an aphakic beneficiary, the
% frames, the add-ons.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule lenses_pseudophakic with provenance Policy Article A52499,
        confer "For beneficiaries with pseudophakia, coverage is limited to one pair of eyeglasses or contact lenses after each cataract surgery with insertion of an IOL":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a refractive lens
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary is pseudophakic
    and the beneficiary is entitled to a pair of lenses after cataract surgery on a date
    and the date of service of the claim is an other date
    and the other date is after or equal to the date.

rule lenses_aphakic with provenance LCD L33793,
        confer "the following lenses or combinations of lenses are covered when determined to be medically necessary":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a refractive lens
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary is aphakic
    and the finding lenses medically necessary about the beneficiary is established.

rule lenses_frames with provenance Policy Article A52499,
        confer "there is no coverage for frames or lens add-on codes unless there is a covered lens(es)":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "V2020"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the device is a covered refractive lens for the beneficiary.

% The add-ons with no criterion of their own.
rule lenses_addons with provenance Policy Article A52499,
        confer "there is no coverage for frames or lens add-on codes unless there is a covered lens(es)":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["V2115", "V2118", "V2121", "V2215", "V2218", "V2219", "V2220", "V2221", "V2315", "V2318", "V2319", "V2320", "V2321", "V2710", "V2715", "V2718", "V2730"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the item is an add-on of a covered lens for the beneficiary.

rule lenses_documented_addons with provenance LCD L33793,
        confer "Anti-reflective coating (V2750), tints (V2744, V2745) or oversize lenses (V2780) are covered only when they are medically necessary for the individual beneficiary and the medical necessity is documented by the treating practitioner":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["V2750", "V2780"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the item is an add-on of a covered lens for the beneficiary
    and the treating practitioner documented the medical necessity of the item for the beneficiary.

rule lenses_tints with provenance LCD L33793,
        confer "Tinted lenses (V2745), including photochromatic lenses (V2744), used as sunglasses, which are prescribed in addition to regular prosthetic lenses to an aphakic beneficiary, will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["V2744", "V2745"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the item is an add-on of a covered lens for the beneficiary
    and the treating practitioner documented the medical necessity of the item for the beneficiary
    and it is not the case that
        the item is used as sunglasses in addition to regular prosthetic lenses.

rule lenses_uv with provenance LCD L33793,
        confer "The addition of UV coating (V2755) is not reasonable and necessary for polycarbonate lenses (V2784)":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "V2755"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the item is an add-on of a covered lens for the beneficiary
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and it is not the case that
        the device carries an impact resistant add-on.

rule lenses_polycarbonate with provenance LCD L33793,
        confer "Lenses made of polycarbonate or other impact-resistant materials (V2784) are covered only for beneficiaries with functional vision in only one eye":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "V2784"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the item is an add-on of a covered lens for the beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has functional vision in only one eye.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The criteria: the diagnosis, the pair after each surgery.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule lenses_diagnosis with provenance Policy Article A52499,
        confer "Covered diagnoses are limited to pseudophakia (condition in which the natural lens has been replaced with an artificial intraocular lens [IOL]), aphakia (condition in which the natural lens has been removed but there is no IOL), and congenital aphakia":
a beneficiary has a covered diagnosis for refractive lenses
    if the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and ICD10 code the code is in group 1 of article "A52499" as a description under table refractive_lenses_icd10.

% Z96.1 is the table's row for pseudophakia; the other rows are aphakia.
rule lenses_pseudophakia with provenance Policy Article A52499,
        confer "pseudophakia (condition in which the natural lens has been replaced with an artificial intraocular lens [IOL])":
a beneficiary is pseudophakic
    if the beneficiary has a covered diagnosis for refractive lenses
    and the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is "Z96.1".

rule lenses_aphakia with provenance Policy Article A52499,
        confer "aphakia (condition in which the natural lens has been removed but there is no IOL), and congenital aphakia":
a beneficiary is aphakic
    if the beneficiary has a covered diagnosis for refractive lenses
    and the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the code is "Z96.1".

rule lenses_one_pair with provenance Policy Article A52499,
        confer "If a beneficiary has a cataract extraction with IOL insertion in one eye, subsequently has a cataract extraction with IOL insertion in the other eye, and does not receive eyeglasses or contact lenses between the two surgical procedures, Medicare covers only one pair of eyeglasses or contact lenses after the second surgery":
a beneficiary is entitled to a pair of lenses after cataract surgery on a date
    if the beneficiary had a cataract extraction with insertion of an intraocular lens on the date
    and it is not the case that
        the beneficiary was furnished a pair of lenses after the date.

section remedy is:

% The policy's own condition of payment (Policy Article A52499, "Policy
% specific documentation requirements").
rule lenses_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52499,
        confer "The diagnosis code that justifies the need for these items must be included on the claim":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is refractive_lenses
    and the claim states the diagnosis code of the beneficiary.
